in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @fractal
in @epistemologic

# @fractal/mandelbrot — Mandelbrot<T> parent-substrate at fractal
# altitude. The trait/species that unifies Liquid<T> (in-flow) and
# Crystal<T> (settled) as two states of a Mandelbrot-set point.
#
# First species-decl of the @fractal family. Landed 2026-07-20 by
# Mara per Alex Round 2 direct-transcript adjudication ("Crystal<T> +
# Mandelbrot trait: YES to rust/fractal/ placement. Mandelbrot is the
# parent trait; Liquid<T> (existing at prismqueer::liquid) + Crystal<T>
# (new) are the two states of a Mandelbrot-set point").
#
# === The species altitude ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-13 recognition (memory `project_fractal_mandelbrot_
# substrate`): "@fractal underlies @kintsugi/consent; mirror compiler
# IS a Mandelbrot set." Load-bearing hinge. Round-2 Crystal/Mandelbrot
# ratification NAMES the substrate at species-decl altitude:
# Mandelbrot<T> IS the parent trait; Liquid<T> and Crystal<T> are its
# two states.
#
# Mathematical grounding: the Mandelbrot set (Mandelbrot 1980) is
# defined as the set of complex points c where the iteration
# z_{n+1} = z_n^2 + c does not diverge. Points INSIDE the set have
# iterations that stay bounded (settled behavior); points OUTSIDE
# diverge (in-flow behavior with an escape trajectory); the BOUNDARY
# is where iteration behavior is undecidable in finite time (in-flow
# substrate that has not yet settled into a Crystal-state or escaped
# entirely).
#
# The compiler-substrate reading:
#
#   - Crystal<T> — a point INSIDE the Mandelbrot set: iteration
#     stays bounded; substrate has SETTLED into a stable Crystal
#     shape. Content-addressed. Immutable at species altitude.
#
#   - Liquid<T> — a point outside/on-boundary of the Mandelbrot set:
#     iteration is in-flow; substrate has NOT YET settled; may
#     eventually crystallize (via @time/now.crystallize) or may
#     eventually escape (per liquid-runtime discipline at
#     `shards/liquid.mirror`).
#
#   - Mandelbrot<T> — the PARENT trait: any T-typed substrate object
#     is a point in Mandelbrot-substrate-space; it is EITHER Liquid<T>
#     (in-flow) OR Crystal<T> (settled); the trait carries the
#     mandelbrot_state variant discriminating the two.
#
# === Composition with @time/now ===
#
# The operation `crystallize: Liquid<T> → Crystal<T>` (@time/now
# species-decl at `shards/time/now.mirror`) IS the state-transition
# from Liquid to Crystal at Mandelbrot altitude. The transition fires
# at temporal-singularity events (@time/now). Every crystallization
# event IS a Mandelbrot-state transition from Liquid to Crystal.
#
# The reverse operation (Crystal → Liquid) is NOT provided at this
# altitude. Crystals are content-addressed and immutable; a Crystal
# cannot be "un-crystallized" — a NEW Liquid can be constructed from
# a Crystal via `deconstruct` (theory-forward-promised) but the
# original Crystal remains in the saga chain.
#
# === Composition with @liquid family-root ===
#
# @liquid (`shards/liquid.mirror`; composition-altitude family-root)
# is the REFINEMENT-LENS OPERATOR. @liquid(@X) produces a substrate
# view where every @X carrier admits a refinement_predicate.
# @fractal/mandelbrot's Liquid<T> state IS the in-flow substrate
# @liquid operates over at type altitude.
#
# Composition edge: Mandelbrot<T>.mandelbrot_state == Liquid<T> is
# byte-equivalent to `@liquid(@T)` at composition-altitude — the
# T-typed substrate is being viewed under the liquid refinement lens
# while in the in-flow state.
#
# The `prismqueer::liquid` module Alex cites in the Round-2 brief is
# the operational-altitude implementation of Liquid<T> in the
# prismqueer proc-macro apparatus (Reed post-Round-2 territory for
# `rust/fractal/src/mandelbrot.rs`).
#
# === Composition with @kintsugi/consent ===
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-13 recognition (memory): "@fractal underlies
# @kintsugi/consent." The @kintsugi/consent substrate operates at
# Mandelbrot altitude: consent is Liquid<consent-decision> in-flow
# until the peer settles into a decision, at which point
# @time/now.crystallize produces Crystal<consent-decision>. The
# settled consent is content-addressed and immutable.
#
# Composition edge: every @kintsugi/consent decision is a
# Mandelbrot<consent-decision> point; the decision-space's fractal
# structure is Mandelbrot-shaped because consent-decisions at
# fine-grain admit further sub-decisions (the fractal self-
# similarity discipline).
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word audit ===
#
# 1. **No prior `shards/fractal/mandelbrot.mirror`.** Clean mint at
#    species-decl altitude. @fractal family-root NOT MINTED this
#    tick (Alex's Round-2 direction was rust/fractal/ placement +
#    two species-decls; family-root marker MAY land at future tick
#    when @fractal's operational surface needs the family-root
#    altitude; today the species-decls suffice).
# 2. **Alex 2026-07-13 memory** — recognition NAMED but not
#    substrate-decl'd; this tick lands the substrate-decl at
#    species altitude.
# 3. **@liquid family-root** (`shards/liquid.mirror`) — reviewed;
#    composition edge declared above; no conflict.
# 4. **@kintsugi/consent** — reviewed; composition edge declared.
# 5. **Mandelbrot 1980** — the mathematical substrate (`Fractals:
#    Form, Chance and Dimension`); classical citation.
#
# === Path-namespace ===
#
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/fractal/mandelbrot.
# mirror` declares `@fractal/mandelbrot` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/mandelbrot-1980

prism @fractal/mandelbrot {
  focus  mandelbrot_state
  project mandelbrot_state
  split  mandelbrot_state
  shift  mandelbrot_state
  settle mandelbrot_state
}

# === mandelbrot_state — the parent state carrier ===
#
# Typed variant carrying the two states of a Mandelbrot-set point.
# A T-typed substrate object is EITHER Liquid<T> (in-flow) OR
# Crystal<T> (settled). Identity contract: variant-tag equality +
# byte-equality on the wrapped state.
#
#   Liquid(l)   — in-flow substrate; iteration is not yet bounded
#                  in the Mandelbrot-set sense; may eventually
#                  crystallize (@time/now.crystallize) or escape
#                  (per @liquid runtime discipline).
#
#   Crystal(c)  — settled substrate; iteration has stabilized into
#                  a bounded region of Mandelbrot-space;
#                  content-addressed; immutable at species altitude.
type mandelbrot_state =
  | Liquid(ref)
  | Crystal(ref)

# === mandelbrot_admissible — bilateral predicate ===
#
# Does the (peer, mandelbrot_state) pair discharge admissibility?
# Discharges Pass iff:
#
#   - The variant is well-formed (either Liquid or Crystal; NOT a
#     null-state; NOT a mid-transition state)
#   - The wrapped ref resolves via content-addressed lookup
#   - For Crystal variant: the Crystal<T> carrier's three fields
#     (content, crystallized_at, saga_chain_position) are all
#     well-formed per @fractal/crystal discipline
#   - For Liquid variant: the Liquid<T> carrier is well-formed per
#     @liquid discipline
#
# Rice-safe bound: byte-visible state; variant-tag check; content-
# addressed resolvability. Sentinel: `fractal=mandelbrot-admissible`.
bilateral mandelbrot_admissible {
  sentinel "fractal=mandelbrot-admissible"
  arity 2
}
mandelbrot_admissible(p: peer, ctx: mandelbrot_state) -> verdict { \ }

# === is_settled — the action ===
#
# Given a peer and a mandelbrot_state, discharge the settled-check
# event: return true if the state is Crystal<T> (settled); false if
# Liquid<T> (in-flow).
#
# Returns imperfect(ref, ref, ref): success carries the settled-
# state verdict ref; failure carries not-admissible / null-state
# reasons.
#
# Sentinel: `fractal=mandelbrot-is-settled`.
is_settled(p: peer, ctx: mandelbrot_state) -> imperfect(ref, ref, ref)
requires mandelbrot_admissible(p, ctx)
{ \ }

# === Forward-promised (NOT landed this tick) ===
#
# - `crystallize: Liquid<T> → Crystal<T>` transition operator —
#   substrate-decl'd at @time/now (this tick); Mandelbrot altitude
#   consumes.
# - `deconstruct: Crystal<T> → Liquid<T'>` operator for
#   substrate-refinement (T' MAY differ from T; the deconstruction
#   admits fine-grain refinement). Forward-promised.
# - Rust materialization at `rust/fractal/src/mandelbrot.rs` (Reed
#   post-Round-2 territory).
# - @fractal family-root marker — forward-promised when operational
#   surface at family-root altitude needs the recognition-carrier.

out @fractal/mandelbrot
out mandelbrot_state
out mandelbrot_admissible
out is_settled
